<title>USA: Mercantile Stores set stock buyback.</title>
<headline>Mercantile Stores set stock buyback.</headline>
<dateline>FAIRFIELD, Ohio 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mercantile Stores Co Inc said Tuesday that its board of directors had authorized the purchase of up to 1.5 million shares of its common stock.</p>
<p>The company said the purchases will be made over a multi-year period, via open market transactions that will be executed on the New York Stock Exchange or otherwise.</p>
<p>The purchased shares will be reserved for issuance on the exercise of options granted under the 1996 stock option plan.</p>
<p>Under this procedure, the exercise of options will not result in any ownership dilution to current shareholders, the company said.</p>
<p>There are currently 36,844,050 shares of common stock outstanding.</p>
